ory> <category>utplsql-core</category> <description>Removed overloaded procedures ut_runner.run · utPLSQL will not not open new transaction when running tests · Added buffering of dbms_output before the run · +8 more</description> <link>https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-v304---released.html</link> <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:29:57 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.utplsql.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">utPLSQL Announcements</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-v304---released.html</guid> </item> <item> <title>We&#39;ve released utPLSQL-cli</title> <category>releases</category> <category>utplsql-core</category> <description>You may find the client on the download page</description> <link>https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/weve-released-utplsql-cli.html</link> <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:29:57 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.utplsql.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">utPLSQL Announcements</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/weve-released-utplsql-cli.html</guid> </item> <item> <title>utPLSQL-cli v3.1.0 released</title> <category>releases</category> <category>utplsql-core</category> <description>Java8 · Oracle JDBC driver file (ojdbc8.jar) is required · Oracle i18n driver file (orai18n.jar) is required for national character-set support · +6 more</description> <link>https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-cli-v310-released.html</link> <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:29:57 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.utplsql.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">utPLSQL Announcements</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-cli-v310-released.html</guid> </item> <item> <title>Better late than never</title> <category>releases</category> <category>utplsql-core</category> <description>On April 25th, a major release 3.1.0 of utPLSQL was published on github and the information was not published on our site.</description> <link>https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/better-late-than-never.html</link> <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:29:57 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.utplsql.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">utPLSQL Announcements</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/better-late-than-never.html</guid> </item> <item> <title>utPLSQL v3.1.2 released</title> <category>releases</category> <category>utplsql-core</category> <description>Added ability to join and compare cursor content by specific columns (PK/UK) · Added support for comma separated list of suite paths/packages when calling ut.run · +23 more</description> <link>https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-v312-released.html</link> <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:29:57 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.utplsql.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">utPLSQL Announcements</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-v312-released.html</guid> </item> <item> <title>utPLSQL-cli v3.1.2 released</title> <category>releases</category> <category>utplsql-cli</category> <description>This version of utPLQL-cli is compatible with all versions of utPLSQL from 3.0.0 to 3.1.3. We encourage you to always use the latest version of cli to communicate with a v3 core.</description> <link>https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-cli-v312-released.html</link> <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:29:57 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.utplsql.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">utPLSQL Announcements</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/utplsql-cli-v312-released.html</guid> </item> <item> <title>How to integrate utPLSQL into Visual Studio</title> <category>tips-n-tricks</category> <description>How to easily integrate @utPLSQL into @VisualStudio via External Tools.</description> <link>https://www.utplsql.org/announcements/how-to-integrate-utplsql-into-visual-studio.html</link> <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:29:57 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.utplsql.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">utPLSQL Announcemen